<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ondonga</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1915 CE (approx.) · capital Olukonda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Ovambo kingdom of northern Namibia and the first to welcome Finnish Lutheran missionaries, whose influence reshaped its society.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ondonga was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people">Ovambo</a> kingdoms on the floodplains south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunene-river">Kunene</a> river, formed by the 17th century under rulers drawn from a royal matriclan. Its people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a>, kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and traded salt from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etosha-pan">Etosha</a> pan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> with neighbours.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The king held wide powers over land and justice and governed through district headmen. Finnish Lutheran missionaries arrived in 1870, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martti-rautanen">Martti Rautanen</a> worked at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olukonda">Olukonda</a>, translating the Bible into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndonga-dialect">Oshindonga</a>. In 1904 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nehale-lyampingana">Nehale lyaMpingana</a>, ruler of eastern Ondonga, attacked the German fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namutoni">Namutoni</a>. Under Martin Elifas, a Christian king who came to power in 1912, Ondonga became largely Christian.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>German colonial claims reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovamboland">Ovamboland</a> but had little effect until <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa">South Africa</a> occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/south-west-africa">South West Africa</a> in 1915, after which the kingdom came under South African administration. Ondonga's kingship survives as a traditional authority in independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1650 CE – 1915 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:5.27%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1915 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Olukonda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kambonde kaMpingana, Nehale lyaMpingana, Martin Elifas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Ovambo religion, Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oshindonga</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/namibia">Namibia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ondonga, Ndonga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1782&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ondonga" aria-label="Kingdom of Ondonga on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5114 2845 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ondonga lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5434 3101L5457 3267M5434 3101L5457 3267"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5457 3267h0M5457 3267h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5434 3101h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5434 3101h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Olukonda. <a href="/atlas?year=1782&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ondonga">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

